WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Have you ever wondered
if there’s a natural way

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.160
to lower your high blood pressure,
guard against Alzheimer's,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.440
lose weight, and feel better?
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.680
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.200
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.560
Did you know that eating a diet
filled with animal products

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.320
can disrupt your microbiome faster
than taking an antibiotic?

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.600
Here’s our first story.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.480
If you go online and search
for Crohn's disease and diet,

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.800
or ulcerative colitis and diet, the
top results are a hodgepodge

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:39.080
of conflicting advice.
What does the science say?

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.960
If you do a systematic review of
the medical literature on dietary

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.400
intake and the risk of developing
inflammatory bowel disease,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:49.000
Crohn's disease is associated
with the intake of fat and meat,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.600
whereas dietary fiber and
fruits appear protective.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.560
The same foods are associated
with the other major inflammatory

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.080
bowel disease, ulcerative
colitis: fat and meat,

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.040
with a protective association
found for vegetable intake.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.960
Why—according to this meta-analysis
of nine separate studies—

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.880
do meat consumers have
about a 50% greater risk

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.840
for inflammatory bowel disease?

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.680
Well, one possibility is that meat
may be a vehicle for bacteria

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.600
that play a role in the development
of such diseases.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.800
Meat contains huge amounts
of Yersinia, for example.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.440
Yes, maybe antibiotic residues
in the meat could be

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:28.640
theoretically kind of mucking
with our microbiome,

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.520
but Yersinia are so-called
psychrotrophic bacteria,

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.280
meaning they're able to grow
at fridge temperatures.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.680
It has been found to be significantly
associated with inflammatory bowel

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.280
disease, supporting this
concept that Yersinia infection

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.120
may be a trigger for chronic
inflammatory bowel disease.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.480
One reason why specifically
animal protein was associated

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.040
with triple the risk of
inflammatory bowel disease—

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.840
but plant protein was not—
is because it can lead

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.000
to the formation of toxic
bacterial end products,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.080
such as the rotten egg
gas, hydrogen sulfide,

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:07.440
which is not just one of the main
malodorous compounds in human

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:12.120
flatus; it's a poison that has been
implicated in ulcerative colitis.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.160
So go on some
meat-heavy, low-carb diet

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:19.280
and we're not just talking about
some malodorous rectal flatus,

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.800
but increased risk of irritable bowel,
inflammatory bowel syndrome,

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.640
and eventually colorectal cancer.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.800
Hydrogen sulfide in the colon comes
from sulphur-containing amino acids

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:34.080
like methionine that are
concentrated in animal proteins,

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.480
though there are also sulfites
added as preservatives

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:40.800
to some nonorganic wine
and nonorganic dried fruit.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.840
But it's the sulphur-containing
amino acids that may be the more

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:47.660
important of the two. Give people
increasing quantities of meat,

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:52.400
and you can get an exponential
rise in fecal sulfides.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.680
Specific bacteria, like Biophilia
wadsworthia, can take this sulfur

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:59.880
that ends up in our colon and
produce hydrogen sulfide.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:03.400
And give people an animal product-
based diet packed with meat

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.520
and eggs and dairy, and
you can specifically increase

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:11.840
the growth of this bacteria. People
underestimate the dramatic effect

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.800
diet can have on our gut bacteria.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.040
Give people a fecal transplant
and it can take three days

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.280
to shift your microbiome.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:22.280
Take a powerful antibiotic like
Cipro and it can take a week.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:26.000
But start packing in the meat and
eggs, and within a single day

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.760
you can change your microbiome—
and not for the better.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:33.040
You can more than double
the bad bacterial machinery

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.240
that churns out hydrogen sulfide,
consistent with the thinking

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.440
that diet-induced changes
to the gut flora may contribute

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.280
to the development of
inflammatory bowel disease.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.560
In other words, the increase in
sulfur compounds in the colon

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.640
when you eat meat is not only
of interest in the field of flatology:

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:54.280
the study of human farts.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:55.160
In our next story,

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:59.520
we look at how plant-based diets
can be 98% effective

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.080
in keeping ulcerative colitis
patients in remission,

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.840
blowing away other treatments.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.560
One of the most common questions
physicians treating patients

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.520
with inflammatory bowel disease
(IBD) are asked is whether

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.160
changing one's diet can positively
affect the course of their disease?

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:19.280
Traditionally, our answer
had been, "We have no clue,"

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.160
but this may now be changing,

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.000
given the evidence that hydrogen
sulfide may be playing

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.480
a role in ulcerative colitis.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:29.720
And since the sulfur-containing
amino acids concentrated in meat

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.960
cause an increase in colonic
levels of this rotten egg gas,

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.600
maybe we should take off the meat.
See, animal protein isn't just associated

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.080
with an increased risk of getting
inflammatory bowel disease

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:46.320
in the first place, but also IBD
relapses once you have the disease.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:51.160
This is a recent development. Because
the concept of IBD as a lifestyle disease

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:55.400
mediated mainly by a Westernized diet
is not widely appreciated, an analysis

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:00.120
of diet in the follow-up period after
diagnosis in relation to a relapse

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:05.520
of inflammatory bowel disease has
been ignored. But not any longer.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:08.880
Ulcerative colitis patients in remission
and their diets were followed for a year

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:13.760
to see which foods were linked to the
bloody diarrhea coming raging back.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:17.960
And the strongest relationship between
a dietary factor and an increased risk

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:23.160
of relapse observed in this study
was for a high intake of meat.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:27.200
So, what if you have people lower
their sulfur-containing amino acid intake

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.640
by decreasing their consumption
of animal products? They tried it

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.960
on four ulcerative colitis patients,
and without any change in meds,

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.720
they experienced like a four-fold
improvement in their loose stools.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:41.080
In fact, they felt so much better
that they didn't think it ethical

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:43.160
to try switching them back.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:47.120
Since sulfur-containing amino acids are
the primary source of dietary sulfur,

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:51.280
a low sulfur diet essentially means
a shift from a typical diet high

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:56.480
in animal protein and fat, and low in
fiber, to more of a plant-based diet.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:58.280
Westernized diets
are pro-inflammatory,

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.880
and plant-based diets
are anti-inflammatory.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:05.760
Let's see what treatment with
a plant-based diet can do, after

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:10.640
the onset of ulcerative colitis during
a low-carbohydrate weight-loss diet.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:14.400
A 36-year-old man lost 13
pounds on a low-carb diet,

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:19.320
but also lost his health,
diagnosed with ulcerative colitis.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:22.480
Put him on a diet centered around
whole plant foods, though,

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:27.520
and poof—symptoms resolved
without medication. Okay, but this is

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.880
just one case. I mean, case reports
are like glorified anecdotes.

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:35.720
The value of case reports lies in
their ability to inspire researchers

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:40.680
to put it to the test, and
that's exactly what they did.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:45.120
There had never been a study published,
focusing on using plant-based diets

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:50.360
for the treatment of
ulcerative colitis until now.

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:53.720
Considering the lack of a suitable
diet to be the biggest issue faced

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.720
in the current treatment of
inflammatory bowel disease,

00:06:55.720 --> 00:07:01.080
and regarding it as a lifestyle disease
caused mainly by our omnivorous diet,

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:05.160
a group of Japanese gastroenterologists
have been providing a plant-based diet

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:10.440
to all patients with IBD for over a
decade, and publishing extraordinary

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:15.920
results, far better than have to date
been reported in the medical literature.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.120
I profiled some of the early work in
one of my first videos that went up

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.360
on NutritionFacts.org, found to
be effective in the maintenance

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.120
of remission in Crohn's disease

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:28.200
by 100% at one year,
90% at two years.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:33.600
So how about a plant-based diet for
relapse prevention in ulcerative colitis?

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:37.160
Educational hospitalization meant
bringing patients into the hospital

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.400
to control their diet
and educate them

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.400
about the benefits
of plant-based eating,

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:44.520
so they'd be more motivated
to continue it at home.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.200
Most patients—about three-quarters—
experienced improvements

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:51.480
such as disappearance or decrease
in bloody stool during hospitalization.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:56.840
Fantastic! Okay, but here's the
really exciting part. Then they followed

00:07:56.840 --> 00:08:01.400
the patients for 5 years, and 81%
were able to remain in remission

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:06.120
the whole time, and 98% were able to keep
the disease at bay for at least a year.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:09.160
I mean that blows other treatments away.

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:12.680
Those relapse rates are far lower
than those reported with medication.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:17.160
Under conventional treatment, other
studies found that about half relapse,

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:21.160
compared to only 2% among
those taught to eat healthier.

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:24.520
A plant-based diet was previously shown
to be effective in both the active and

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:28.440
quiescent stages of Crohn's disease.
The current study has shown that a

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:31.320
plant-based diet is effective in both
the active and quiescent stages

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.600
of ulcerative colitis as well.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:37.760
And so they did another study on
even more severely affected cases

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:40.920
with active disease
and found the same thing,

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.280
far beating out
conventional drug therapy.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:47.680
People felt so much better, they
were still eating more plant-based

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.200
even 6 years later.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:52.360
The researchers conclude that
a plant-based diet is effective

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:56.080
for treating ulcerative colitis
to prevent a relapse.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:00.200
Why? Well, plant-based diets are rich
in fiber, which feeds our good gut bugs.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.720
That might partly explain why
a plant-based diet prevents

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:05.080
a variety of chronic diseases.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:08.000
And so that's what we may be seeing
with inflammatory bowel disease,

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.480
suggesting that replacing an omnivorous
diet with a plant-based diet

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:15.400
is the right approach. It's like using
plant-based diets to treat

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:18.040
the cause of heart
disease, our #1 killer.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:22.120
Not just safer and cheaper,
but works better.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.880
No adverse side effects
noted for plant-based eating.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:28.320
Let's compare that to the side
effects of immunosuppressants

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:31.400
used for ulcerative colitis, like
cyclosporine. Side effects include...

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:36.600
And now we have even fancier drugs
that cost about $60,000 a year

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:40.640
that s $5,000 a month and
they don't even work very well,

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.040
with clinical remission at 1 year
of only like 17 to 34%.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:49.880
And instead of no adverse side
effects, they can give you a stroke.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:53.840
They can give you heart failure.
They can even give you cancer,

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:58.640
including a rare type of cancer
that often results in death.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:02.360
Or how about a serious brain disease
known as progressive multifocal

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:05.360
leukoencephalopathy,
which can kill you,

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:08.840
and for which there is
no known treatment or cure.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:11.040
Yeah, yeah, increased risk of death,

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:18.080
but did we mention how nice and small
the pill was and the easy-to-open bottle?

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:18.800
Finally today,

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:21.040
we look at how switching
to a plant-based diet

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:22.600
has been shown to achieve
far better outcomes

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:25.080
than those reported on
conventional treatments

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:28.720
in both active and quiescent stages
in both Crohn’s disease

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:31.360
and ulcerative colitis.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:34.400
Important to our understanding
and prevention of the global increase

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:39.760
in inflammatory bowel disease, we know
that dietary fiber appears to reduce risk,

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:44.760
whereas dietary fat, animal protein,
and sugar may increase risk.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.440
"Despite the recognition of the
westernization of lifestyle as

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:52.000
a major driver of the growing incidence
of inflammatory bowel disease,

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:56.200
no countermeasures against such lifestyle
changes have been recommended,

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:59.400
except that patients with Crohn's
disease shouldn't smoke."

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.160
Look, we know consuming
whole, plant-based foods

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:05.419
is synonymous with an
anti-inflammatory diet.

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:10.480
So how about putting a
plant-based diet to the test?

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:14.680
Just cutting down on red and
processed meat didn't work,

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:18.080
but what about cutting
down on all meat?

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:20.600
A 25-year-old guy diagnosed
with Crohn's disease,

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:25.560
but failed to enter clinical remission
despite standard medical therapy.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:29.240
But after switching to a diet based
exclusively on grains, legumes—

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:32.160
like beans, split peas, chickpeas,
and lentils—vegetables, and fruits,

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:35.480
he entered clinical remission,
without the need for medication

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:39.840
and showed no signs of Crohn's
disease on follow-up colonoscopy.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:42.920
It's worth delving into
some of the details.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:48.080
The conventional treatment they started
him on is infliximab, sold as REMICADE,

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:52.320
which can cause a stroke, and may
increase your chances of getting

00:11:52.320 --> 00:12:00.440
lymphoma and other cancers—but
it's a bargain for only $35,000 a year.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:04.600
And it may not even work
in 35 to 40% of patients,

00:12:04.600 --> 00:12:09.040
and that seemed to be the case
here, so they upped the dose

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:13.800
after 37 weeks, and still suffering
after two years on the drug—

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:17.160
until he tried completely eliminating
animal products and processed foods

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:23.760
from his diet—finally experiencing
a complete resolution of his symptoms.

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:27.400
Prior to this, his diet had
been a typical American diet.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:31.360
But having experienced complete
clinical remission for the first time

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:35.400
since his diagnosis, he decided
to switch to a whole-food,

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:39.560
plant-based diet permanently, severely
reducing his intake of processed food

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:43.760
and limiting animal products
to one serving, or less, per week.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:48.800
And whenever his diet started to slip,
symptoms started coming back.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:51.840
But he could always wipe
them out by eating healthier.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:54.680
After six months of implementing
these changes in diet and lifestyle,

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:59.320
including stress relief and exercise,
a follow-up demonstrated complete

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:04.760
mucosal healing of the gut lining with
no visible evidence of Crohn's disease.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:08.160
We know a diet consisting of whole
grains, legumes, fruits, and vegetables

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:11.040
has been shown to be helpful in the
prevention and treatment of heart

00:13:11.040 --> 00:13:14.720
disease, obesity, diabetes,
hypertension, gallbladder disease,

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:16.960
rheumatoid arthritis,
and many cancers.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.640
Although further research is required,
this case report suggests

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:23.920
that Crohn's disease might be
added to this list of conditions.

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:27.120
But that further research
has already been done!

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:31.080
About 20 patients with Crohn's disease
were placed on a semi-vegetarian diet,

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.400
meaning no more than a half-
serving of fish once a week

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:37.360
and a half-serving of meat
once every two weeks,

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:42.560
and achieved 100% remission rate
at one year, and 90% at two years.

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:46.560
Some strayed from the diet though.
Let's see what happened to them.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:52.320
After a year, half had relapsed, and at
year two only 20% remained in remission.

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:55.960
But those that stuck with
it had remarkable success.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:58.800
It was a small study with
no formal control group,

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:03.280
but represents the best reported
result in Crohn's relapse prevention

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:07.160
published in the medical
literature to date.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:10.680
Nowadays, Crohn's patients are often
treated with so-called biologic drugs,

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:14.760
expensive injected antibodies that
suppress your immune system

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:18.120
and have effectively induced
and maintained remission

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:20.960
in Crohn's disease,
but not in everyone.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:25.640
The current remission rate in Crohn's
with early use of REMICADE: 64%.

00:14:25.640 --> 00:14:31.120
So 30 to 40% of patients are likely to
experience a disabling disease course

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:36.080
even after treatment. So what
about adding a plant-based diet?

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:40.880
Remission rates jumped up to 100%
for those who didn't have to drop out

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:45.120
due to drug side effects. Even
if you exclude the milder cases,

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:51.440
100% of those with serious, even severe
fulminant disease achieved remission.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:54.280
But if you look at gold standard
systematic reviews, they conclude

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:58.120
that the effects of dietary interventions
on inflammatory bowel diseases,

00:14:58.120 --> 00:15:02.040
Crohn's disease and ulcerative
colitis, are uncertain.

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:05.160
This is because only randomized
controlled trials were considered.

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:08.920
Totally understandable, as that's
the most rigorous study design.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:12.720
Nevertheless, people with inflammatory
bowel disease deserve advice

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:17.760
based on the 'best available evidence'
rather than no advice at all.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:20.360
And switching to a plant-based diet
has been shown to achieve

00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:24.160
far better outcomes than those
reported on conventional treatments

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:29.430
in both active and quiescent stages
in both Crohn's and ulcerative colitis.

00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:34.680
Maybe we should recommend plant-based
diets for inflammatory bowel disease.

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:38.080
It would seem clear that treatment
based on treating the cause

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.120
of the disease is optimal.

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:43.240
Spreading the word about healthier
diets could help halt the scourge

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:46.600
of inflammatory bowel, but how
are people going to hear about

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:51.240
this amazing research without some
kind of public education campaign?

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:56.640
That's what NutritionFacts.org
is all about.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:59.080
